# lab.env: one per campaign at $LAB_DIR/lab.env; every harness script sources it.
# Copy: cp lab.env.example ~/lab/<campaign>/lab.env, then edit. Values here are the defaults.
# A value set here overrides the caller's environment for that variable: with NIC_MODEL set in
# this file, `NIC_MODEL=vmxnet3 vm-clone ...` is ignored. Leave a variable out to let the
# environment (or the built-in default) decide.
LAB_DIR=$HOME/lab/CAMPAIGN          # replace CAMPAIGN
VM_PREFIX=CAMPAIGN-                 # every VM of this campaign starts with it; scripts refuse other names
LAB_USER=ubuntu                     # guest user for vm-ssh / vm-sudo (VM_USER=... overrides per call)
#PASSFILE=$LAB_DIR/secrets/vm-pass  # guest sudo password file (mode 600), if sudo needs a password
#SECRETS=$LAB_DIR/secrets           # directory (mode 700) of secret files (one value per file); scrub-evidence searches the evidence for their lines
#EVID=$LAB_DIR/evidence
#IMG=/var/lib/libvirt/images        # root-only (711): scripts use sudo for writes and globs there
#SCSI_MODEL=virtio-scsi             # boot disk controller; OVMF cannot boot vmpvscsi
#NIC_MODEL=virtio                   # vmxnet3 for VMware-like guests
#MAX_RUNNING_GB=25                  # vm-create refuses to exceed this (25 on a typical 32 GiB host: it reports a little under 32)
                                    # Default when unset: derived from host RAM in GiB minus 6 (minus 2 on hosts of
                                    # 8 GiB or less), floor 4; 24 if RAM cannot be read. Counts only running
                                    # guests; `virsh start` of a stopped VM bypasses it.
#DEPLOY=http://192.168.122.1        # nginx deploy server as seen from guests on the default network
#NGINX_LOG=/var/log/nginx/deploy-access.log   # adds a request counter to wait-ready heartbeats
